---
title: "Install on Android with Termux"
description: Build and run KoboldCpp on an Android phone or tablet with Termux and the official quick setup script.
sidebar:
  label: "Android (Termux)"
  order: 5
---

On Android, KoboldCpp runs inside the Termux terminal app and is compiled on the device. An official script does the setup for you.

{% steps %}

1. Install [Termux from F-Droid](https://f-droid.org/en/packages/com.termux/).

2. Open Termux and run the setup script:

   ```sh {% title="Termux" frame="terminal" %}
   curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/concedo/android_install.sh | sh
   ```

   Run this way, the script installs KoboldCpp and starts it with a small Gemma3-1B model.

3. When it has loaded, open `http://localhost:5001` in your phone's browser.

{% /steps %}

## Choosing a different model

Download the script and run it yourself to get a menu:

```sh {% title="Termux" frame="terminal" %}
curl -sSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/concedo/android_install.sh
chmod +x android_install.sh
./android_install.sh
```

| Option | What it does |
|---|---|
| 1 | Install and launch with Gemma3-1B |
| 2 | Install without a model |
| 3 | Download a GGUF model from a URL |
| 4 | Load a GGUF model that is already on the device |
| 5 | Exit |

Options 3 and 4 need an existing install. Run them from the `koboldcpp` folder, which has its own copy of the script. Option 4 only lists `.gguf` files in that folder.

```sh {% title="Termux" frame="terminal" %}
cd koboldcpp
bash android_install.sh
```

Use a small model. See [Choose a model](/getting-started/model/).

## What the script does

1. Stops if it is not running on Android.
2. If `wget`, `git` or `python` is missing, runs `apt update`, installs `openssl`, `wget`, `git` and `python`, and runs `pkg upgrade`.
3. Clones the KoboldCpp repository, unless it finds an existing copy.
4. Compiles it with `make -j 2`, unless a build already exists.
5. Starts it with `python koboldcpp.py --model <model>`.

## Updating

Running the script again does **not** rebuild KoboldCpp: it skips compiling when a build already exists. To update, pull the new source and compile it again:

```sh {% title="Termux" frame="terminal" %}
cd koboldcpp
git pull
make
```

## Advanced: manual setup

```sh {% title="Termux" frame="terminal" %}
pkg update
pkg upgrade
pkg install openssl wget git python clang make
git clone https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp.git
cd koboldcpp
make
python koboldcpp.py --model mymodel.gguf
```

Download a small GGUF model into the folder first, or pass a model URL to `--model`. Then open `http://localhost:5001`.

- **Packages fail to install:** run `termux-change-repo` and pick another mirror.
- **`Illegal instruction` on your device:** rebuild with `make clean`, then `make LLAMA_PORTABLE=1`, which turns off tuning for your specific processor.
- **GPU:** these instructions cover CPU builds. GPU acceleration depends on the device and its drivers.

More: [OS-specific problems](/docs/troubleshooting/os-specific/#android-illegal-instruction).

